(OPR-37 (undocumented precision): shift counts are taken modulo 64.
 Shifting by 64 is a no-op (64 mod 64 is 0) and shifting by 100 shifts
 by 36. A negative count wraps the same way: -2 becomes 62, so
 16 bit-shift-right -2 is 0. LANGUAGE.md:4843-4844 states no bound on
 the shift count. This is memory-safe but it is a wrong-answer trap for
 any leaf that asserts a shift result without clamping its count.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox OPR-37.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1
   68719476736
   0
)
a number called 'single bit' is 1.
Print 'single bit' bit-shift-left 64.
Print 'single bit' bit-shift-left 100.
a number called payload is 16.
a number called 'negative places' is 0 subtract 2.
Print payload bit-shift-right 'negative places'.
